s5.condition:
The entry s5 matters only if the 0x1000 bit of the flags halfword (at DC+0xA, where DC is the word at arg1+0xDC) is clear when read at 0x80117130 and set, with bit 0x8000 clear, when read again at 0x80117198. Two other conditions must also hold: func_801108A8 (0x80117180) returns nonzero, and arg1+0xEA is nonzero. The only thing that can flip the bit is a write landing on arg1+0xDC or DC+0xA during func_801108A8. Its writes go to:
- the texture-cache slot it DMAs and decompresses into (0x80143CA0+n*0x830 with n<6, or 0x80146DC0+n*0x1830 with n<3);
- its heap scratch buffer;
- the slot tables at 0x8014B650-0x8014B674;
- resource-pool entries;
- this frame's sp+0x34/sp+0x38.
So the descriptor or arg1's DC field would have to lie inside one of those areas. The other way is a concurrent thread or interrupt rewriting the flags between 0x80117130 and 0x80117198, or between 0x80117198 and 0x8011725C for the read at 0x80117298. In either case s5 is then dereferenced at 0x801171BC/0x801171DC/0x80117298, and the halfwords it loads feed the arguments of func_800DACD8, func_800DB2A4 and func_800DB9E8, and the display-list choice made at 0x801172F4/0x80117300.
